    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d317-a3">

                <pb facs="0576" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg448"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 961.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Lord Granville</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 4,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    reception of your lordship’s note of the 31st ultimo, informing me that Her
                    Majesty would be pleased to accept the return of the Alert, and stating the
                    cordial and friendly manner in which Her Majesty reciprocates the action of my
                    Government in this matter.</p>
                <p>I shall take great pleasure in sending, by the earliest opportunity, a copy of
                    this correspondence to the Department of State.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
